const readTone = computed<ReadTone>(() => {
  const rec = recovery.value;
  const form = tsb.value ?? 0;
  if (rec != null && rec >= 70 && form >= 0) return "strong";
  if (rec != null && rec < 50) return "low";
  return "balanced";
});
```
SQL (prod, last 180 days, n=137 scored days):
• 76 of 137 days (55.5%) score below 50, i.e. the app says "recovery is low" on the majority of days.
• Median absolute day-over-day change in recovery_score: **15.6 points** on a scale whose only threshold is at 50.
• The hero verdict (strong/balanced/low, recomputed from stored recovery_score and tsb) changes on **56 of 98 consecutive-day pairs — 57.1%**. A fair coin flipping between two states changes 50% of the time.
• Nightly HRV over the same window: mean 17.68 ms, SD 5.50 ms. A 7-day rolling mean of the same series has SD 2.46 ms — the smoothing removes 55% of the spread, which is the whole reason Garmin uses a 7-day average.
